 <dialog id="about-dialog" aria-labelledby="about-title"><button class="dialog-close quiet" data-close="about-dialog" aria-label="Close how it works">×</button><p class="eyebrow">UNDER THE LENS</p><h2 id="about-title">Useful signals.<br>Honest limits.</h2><p>Messages, calls, links and emails use inspectable English-language rules. We look for risky requests and address structure. We don’t visit links, authenticate pasted email headers, or identify a caller from their voice.</p>
 <h3>A link can say one thing and point elsewhere</h3><p>For HTML emails, we compare a displayed web address with the link’s actual host. A difference is observable, but legitimate tracking links can differ too. Plain pasted text and screenshots can hide the underlying link. We do not follow redirects or inspect a website’s reputation.</p>
 <h3>Screenshots: read, then review</h3><p>Windows OCR extracts English text locally. Review and correct it before analysis. It can miss or misread words and links, especially small text. It does not establish who sent the message.</p>
-<h3>Images: two separate checks</h3><p>Content Credentials checks a file’s signed C2PA declarations against a local trust snapshot. A valid signature binds a statement to the file; it does not make everything depicted true. Missing credentials don’t prove anything about origin.</p><p>The optional local image detector examines visual patterns. Its output is experimental. AI-origin evidence is not a fraud verdict.</p><h3>What has actually been measured?</h3><p>This app retains the existing CLIP / CommunityForensics runtime. Its older 670-image benchmark reported 95.07% binary classification accuracy; that is not 95% useful definite answers or a real-world guarantee.</p><p>A separate experimental model reached 99.24% / 98.74% on examined development data, then 95.40% / 95.85% on fresh OpenFake and 92.46% / 92.12% on Arena (original / JPEG60, correct definite answers divided by all sources). It failed the release rules and is <strong>not installed here</strong>.</p><p>No accuracy claim is made for scam detection. The practice examples are educational scenarios, not an independent benchmark.</p><h3>Your data</h3><p>Checks run on the local server on this computer. Uploads may use temporary files, removed after processing. The app does not retain inputs or call a remote analysis service. Clearing removes the input and result from this page. A selected download saves only the generic, input-free action summary.</p><button class="primary" data-close="about-dialog">Back to the checker</button></dialog>
+<h3>Images: two separate checks</h3><p>Content Credentials checks a file’s signed C2PA declarations against a local trust snapshot. A valid signature binds a statement to the file; it does not make everything depicted true. Missing credentials don’t prove anything about origin.</p><p>The optional local image detector examines visual patterns. Its output is experimental. AI-origin evidence is not a fraud verdict.</p><h3>What has actually been measured?</h3><p>The optional CLIP / CommunityForensics image detector has not passed our release requirements. Historical evaluations of its decision policy left many images inconclusive and fell well below the required rate of correct definite answers. Its older 670-image binary score does not describe today's useful answer rate or real-world accuracy.</p><p>Use image results as limited clues. Verify the publisher, context and any payment request independently. No replacement model passed all release requirements; none was installed.</p><p>No accuracy claim is made for scam detection. The practice examples are educational scenarios, not an independent benchmark. Detailed historical results and their limitations are in the bundled evaluation notes.</p><h3>Your data</h3><p>Checks run on the local server on this computer. Uploads may use temporary files, removed after processing. The app does not retain inputs or call a remote analysis service. Clearing removes the input and result from this page. A selected download saves only the generic, input-free action summary.</p><button class="primary" data-close="about-dialog">Back to the checker</button></dialog>
