+# What the evidence supports
+
+## Shipping runtime
+
+The image path retains `clip_community_v1`, classifier cutoff 0.35, and its existing model-disagreement abstention policy. Model metadata SHA256: `b2edf1191d09e6fd27fe97187f100de9e1f2cb6158495ceb127435b86d0f3860`. This is the same runtime as the earlier installed app. This build improves the product workflow, not its trained parameters.
+
+Its historical 670-image clean benchmark reported 95.0746% **binary classifier** accuracy. The result predates the inconclusive display policy, uses known generator groups and is not a guarantee for arbitrary images. The UI's limitations disclose this distinction. The source package retains its metadata and JPEG60 robustness report.
+
+## Separate experimental candidate, not installed
+
+PE_adapted_71401 measured 99.24% original and 98.74% JPEG60 correct definite/all on 6,038 examined development sources. Those development numbers are not independent release performance.
+
+| Frozen independent evaluation | Original correct definite/all | JPEG60 correct definite/all |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Fresh balanced OpenFake, 6,068 sources | 5,789 / 6,068 = 95.40% | 5,816 / 6,068 = 95.85% |
+| Fixed Arena, 2,030 sources | 1,877 / 2,030 = 92.46% | 1,870 / 2,030 = 92.12% |
+
+Only two of the four required example views passed. The candidate failed acceptance, was not installed, and was not retried on another supposedly fresh allocation in this build. Historical report identifier: `training-v2-generalization-20261013/release-request-20261016/REPORT.md`.
+
+## This product build
+
+Software tests check known behavior, error cases, trust boundaries and privacy. Actual native C2PA signing/tampering tests establish verification behavior for constructed fixtures. A real CPU image request establishes that the frozen runtime loads and executes. It uses a constructed geometric image and establishes no accuracy.
+
+Scam-text rules have **no measured population accuracy**, calibrated probability, or real-world false-positive-rate claim. Unit tests include ordinary code notifications and warnings because false accusations matter, but a small hand-written set cannot establish generalization. No user study has been completed. English is the only supported rule language.
+
+Do not advertise “99% accurate,” “fraud-proof,” “detects all AI,” “verifies a caller,” or “C2PA proves a transaction safe.” Useful future evaluation would measure safe next-step selection and false reassurance in a consent-based community pilot, followed by an independently labeled corpus with clear scope and uncertainty.
+
+## October 23 installed-policy audit
+
+The read-only audit completed under `accuracy-request-20261023` in the original project's sprint artifacts. Historical cached-feature reconstructions explicitly linked to the installed metadata and disagreement policy recorded only 51.80% original and 48.59% JPEG60 correct definite/all on one examined 6,942-source OpenFake cohort; its saved Arena report recorded 33.40% and 20.30% on 2,030 sources. Many cases were inconclusive. These were historical reconstructions, not newly verified native Torch inference or representative population estimates. Other historical cohorts also fell well below the release target. The older binary score above must not be used as today's useful-answer rate.
+
+No eligible installed-v1 release freeze or approved native evaluation runner was identified. No sealed final was opened or recomputed. Before any new evaluation, review fitting/calibration overlap, admitted licenses and roles, exact runtime parity, prior exposure and resource guards. Failed replacement candidates remain rejected and the language pilot's development split remains unscored.
